				<wikidot:authorName>Monteparnas</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2926286</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Classification is a tricky proposal. I would say that Ringo is actually Euclid, but it doesn't mean he can be kept by WWS because he still needs a rather specialized and expensive set of containment procedures.</p> <p>But otherwise, I got your point. I don't totally agree with, but it makes some sense to have a distinct approach to WWS in the beginning.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6707970#post-4246686</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6707970/critter-profile:ringo#post-4246686</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 12 May 2019 17:42:04 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>HotColes</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3997195</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Eh. This GoI format was posted when there wasn't a lot of lore about WWS just yet, up until the OCT contest I'm pretty sure there were only 2 tales posted using WWS and Ringo was the 4th of the Critter Profile formats. Since this was posted there's been quite a few things that Darkstuff/Nicolini have done that have expanded the lore of WWS by quite a bit.</p> <p>My personal interpretation when I created this article was that the Foundation never intended/expected a terrorist group to target WWS since most of their anomalies are harmless. I tried to establish that the Foundation technically had to let WWS hold Ringo at first due to it being unspecified in the Boring agreement, but with time it became clear that Ringo was in Keter territory.</p> <p>I've sprinkled in a little bit of world-building in one of my other articles about the CI somewhat targeting WWS after Ringo came to light. :p</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6707970#post-4245642</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-6707970/critter-profile:ringo#post-4245642</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 11 May 2019 16:45:43 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Monteparnas</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2926286</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I sincerely think WWS should have more information on other GOIs. As a somewhat independent ally to the Foundation, this kind of information is crucial, so they have some training on how to deal with any approach from other GOIs.</p> <p>MC&amp;Dark is a prime candidate for frequent harassment of WWS, together with CI, but even CotBG and Wondertainment can come into contact for a reason or other, be it peaceful or hostile contact.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
